+    to a renaming of its regions) projects the value given back to the ignored
+    borrows of R, and its own children continue from there: the positions of a
+    projection are those whose path takes the given-back side exactly at the
+    ignored borrows of the regions which ended on the way to it. E.g., for
+    [O<'a, 'b, 'c> { w : &'a mut W<'b, 'c> }], [W<'b, 'c> { c : &'b mut C<'c> }]
+    and the region ['c] at relative level 1: the child created when ['a] ended
+    holds the path [g.c], the one created when ['b] ended the path [c.g]. We
+    keep the projections whose positions are all selected and replace those
+    whose positions are not selected with [AEmpty] (they are not translated at
+    this level).
